// TEST: A function of an index passed where the body applies the parameter
// ============================================================================
// Was a refusal (BL3001 at the argument): `c(0)` decided `c` was an ARRAY the
// moment the body applied it, so a function of an index could not be passed.
// Now LEGAL. An array is a function of its indices (dimensional currying), so
// applying an unannotated parameter to an integer says only that it is an
// ARROW -- the argument decides the kind: here a function of an Int64, so the
// application is a call and the lambda's parameter is typed Int64.
let g = lambda(i) -> 10.0 * Float64(i)
function first(c) = c(0) + 1.0
let d = first(g)
// EXPECT: d = 1
let e = first(lambda(i) -> 10.0 * Float64(i + 2))
// EXPECT: e = 21
